<title>USA: AMBAC qualfies 15 muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualfies 15 muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp said it has qualified for bond insurance the following 15 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Van Buren S.D. #42, Ark., $4.150 million construction bonds.</p>
<p>--Mesa Unified S.D. #4, Ariz., $14.750 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Lake County, Ill., $11 million water and sewer bonds.</p>
<p>--Champlin, Minn., $795,000 general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Champlin, Minn., Economic Development, $3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Alamogordo, N.M., $5.7 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Las Cruces, N.M., $3.260 million general purpose bonds.</p>
<p>--Kendall Central Sch., N.Y., $6.350 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Berkeley County S.D., S.C., $9.3 million school building bonds.</p>
<p>--Beaumont, Texas, $28.88 million refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--Timberlake Improvment District, Texas, $2.180 million (tax) GOs.</p>
<p>--Olympia S.D. #111, Wash., $23 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Dunn County, Wis., $6.555 million building GOs.</p>
<p>--Sussex, Wis., $2.6 water system mortgage revenue bonds as a direct purchase.</p>
<p>--Bowie County, Texas, $2.270 million bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
